# Non-recursive type aliases continue to work correctly.
# [Point: [type [x: Integer  y: Integer]]] produces an Intersection body in the type system.
# At runtime, the type alias evaluates to an empty dict.
# Usage: [@Point [x: 1  y: 2]] checks the dict satisfies the Point type.
[
  Point: [type [x: Integer  y: Integer]]
  p: [@Point [x: 3  y: 4]]
]
=== out
["Point": []  "p": ["x": 3  "y": 4]]
